# Moto G 2026 Root Guide

Here are the steps I took to root my Moto G 2026. I'm sharing this so that anyone who wants to can actually own their phone.

Government mass surveillance is intrusive and oppressive. Data that is gathered and stored indefinitely can be used against you. It's used to take money out of your pocket and can even influence whether you get to live or die. For real.

Your device build and security update level must match exactly. If they don't, you'll need to obtain the correct firmware yourself. First, unlock the bootloader and download your exact firmware through Motorola's website.

The `vbmeta_disabled.img` was created with:

```bash
avbtool make_vbmeta_image --flags 2 --output vbmeta_disabled.img
```

Once you have patched `init_boot.img` and disabled AVB (by flashing `vbmeta` and `vbmeta_system` with the disable flags), you're free to flash `init_boot`.

Verification will fail if the size of the image you're writing doesn't exactly match the size of the existing `init_boot.img`. The next set of commands pads the image so that it matches byte-for-byte. After that, the image will flash successfully and the device will boot with root access.

**Device Name:** Moto G 2026 (128 GB)
**RAM:** 4 GB + 4 GB (RAM Boost)
**Android:** 16
**Network Lock:** Unlocked
**Build:** W1WN36.18-114
**Host Machine:** Arch Linux (amd64)

```
SW Version: nevada_g_sys-user 16 W1WN36.18-114
MBM Version: MBM-3.1-nevada_g_vext-e781a-W1WN36.18-114-d2725
Modem Version: MT6835N_NR17.RC.MP.V18.6.6.P133.02.337R
SW Display Build ID: W1WN36.18-114
```

## Warning

Unlocking the bootloader and rooting your device may:

* Void your warranty
* Factory reset your device
* Cause boot loops if done incorrectly
* Disable some security features

Proceed at your own risk.

